So, this will fall under the law, the Quranic law, that you may dislike something when it is good for you.

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.000
Or you may like something which is bad for you.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:19.000
So, the moral is, we must submit to God totally, completely. Whatever is happening, we have to accept it.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:22.000
We have to know that it is for your own good.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:26.000
If you're a believer, then whatever is happening is for your own good.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.000
17.

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:34.000
I think we've got to stop here because of the workers are going to work.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:37.000
7 o'clock. Susan, wake up.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.000
You're supposed to go have breakfast and go to work.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.000
Why don't you go ahead?

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.000
Lisa, you wanna help her find something in there?

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:54.000
Lisa is not working today.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:57.000
You're the only one.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.000
Dr. Khalifa: We'll see you, IN SHAA ALLAH, what, at noon?

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:00.000
Susan: I have a one.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.000
Dr. Khalifa: For the Noon Prayer? Great.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: Have a great morning. Susan: I have a one.

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:05.000
Dr. Khalifa: Hmm? Susan: I have a one.

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, I know.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.000
Dr. Khalifa: Let's read 17.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:16.000
[28:17] He said, "My Lord, in return for Your blessings upon me, I will never be a supporter of the guilty ones."

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:21.000
[28:18] In the morning, he was in the city, afraid and watchful. ...

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:24.000
He didn't know if his crime has been exposed or not.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:27.000
[28:18] ... The one who sought his help the day before,...

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:30.000
is a troublemaker. And he asked him for help again.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.000
[28:18] ... Moses said to him, "You are really a troublemaker."

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:36.000
Today, he was fighting again with an Egyptian.

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:39.000
And his name was Wakili.

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:41.000
Moses' Crime Exposed

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:45.000
A man: What? Dr. Khalifa: Number 19.

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: We know somebody called Wakili and he fights with anything that comes in his way. Yes.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:55.000
God shows us examples of everything.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Moses' Crime Exposed

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:13.000
[28:19] Before he attempted to strike their common enemy, he said, "O Moses, do you want to kill me, like you killed the other man yesterday? Obviously, you wish to be a tyrant on earth; you do not wish to be righteous."

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:19.000
So, this tells us that now everybody knows that he killed an Egyptian.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:28.000
[28:20] A man came running from the other side of the city, saying, "O Moses, the people are plotting to kill you. You better leave immediately. I am giving you good advice."

00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:34.000
[28:21] He fled the city, afraid and watchful. He said, "My Lord, save me from the oppressive people."

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:46.000
Of course, we know the rest of this. This led to his marriage and his return to Egypt as a hero with God's message.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:48.000
Alhamdu Lillah

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:50.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yeah. Go ahead.

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:54.000
Parivash: Did he kill him by accident or was he angry? Dr. Khalifa: It was an accident.

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:58.000
Dr. Khalifa: It was accident. Yes. Actually he didn't kill him, God killed him.

00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:01.000
Everything was timed that way.

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:09.000
Dr. Khalifa: We know about Moses, he was hot-tempered and he was physically very strong.

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:17.000
A man: I think the whole thing was done keeping with God's plan. Dr. Khalifa: Exactly.

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:24.000
I mean, look here. This is a simple history, but there are so many lessons that we learn from it.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:29.000
Because God's power is illustrated in every, every sentence.

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: Behrouz, you're here! You're home! Behrouz: Yes, sir. Yes. Alhamdu Lillah. Dr. Khalifa: Mã Shã Allãh.

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: Parivash is shaking her head because we lost the guy. Now, he's in Tucson.

00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:52.000
Dr. Khalifa: We will come and visit him now. There's one more reason for them to come and visit Tucson.

00:23:54.000 --> 00:24:01.000
Behrouz: Last week, we were talking about the children of Israel.

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:08.000
Behrouz: These people must be very different with other creatures in the world because of the miracles that God showed them.

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:15.000
Behrouz: And even Moses was the only prophet, actually went to see God.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:24.000
You know, like everybody at that time, they were asking for more miracles. 9 miracles they had.

00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:30.000
Behrouz: And even Moses wanted to see God himself, I mean.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: But you know, it happened because he was speaking with God.

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:34.000
Behrouz: Right.

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:39.000
Dr. Khalifa: And it's a natural curiosity in that situation. Because, suppose I'm speaking to you and you're invisible.

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: Then, I will want to see you. Behrouz: (unintelligible)

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:46.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, so, it was in the conversation.

00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:52.000
But the children of Israel wanted to see God, but it was a totally different issue. It was out of defiance.

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:55.000
They said "We will not believe unless we see God physically", they said.

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: But the situation with Moses was different. He was...

00:24:57.000 --> 00:25:00.000
Edip: He was challenging, Moses only...

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:05.000
Dr. Khalifa: Moses was in the conversation. He said "my Lord, let me see You."

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:07.000
(7:143) رَبِّ أَرِنِىٓ أَنظُرْ إِلَيْكَ

00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:09.000
"My lord, let me look at You and see You."

00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:17.000
Behrouz: It was not because of this kind of nation that they didn't believe.

00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right. Behrouz: They wanted more miracles and more miracles. Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:24.000
Dr. Khalifa: That was the ultimate defiance. That's what they did.

00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:31.000
Edip: But Rashad, at that time, there were about 70 people around him who took them to...

00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:33.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, no, no, no. That's different.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: The 70 men went to apologize.

00:25:39.000 --> 00:25:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: This was back in the camp.

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:45.000
They were all in Sinai and they thought they will not believe "unless we see God physically." So, they died.

00:25:46.000 --> 00:25:48.000
Because God showed them a little bit.

00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:51.000
And they died.

00:25:52.000 --> 00:25:53.000
Then, God revived them.

00:25:55.000 --> 00:25:57.000
One of the incidents in the Quran where God revived the dead.

00:25:58.000 --> 00:26:04.000
But with Moses, this was done actually, it was computerized to teach us that this earth cannot stand the presence of God.

00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:06.000
Because God wiped out the mountain.

00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:10.000
Just to... It was a fact.

00:26:10.000 --> 00:26:14.000
I mean, God manifested Himself to the mountain. And the mountain shattered.

00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:21.000
And Moses fell unconscious. Then, when he came to, the first thing he said "Subhanak (سُبْحَـٰنَكَ)", Glory be to You.

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:24.000
I apologize. Sorry.

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:29.000
I'm ignorant.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:36.000
Parivash: His intention, his intention was like Abraham when he asked, he didn't believe them. Dr. Khalifa: Yes. Exactly.

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:38.000
Dr. Khalifa: Exactly.

00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:42.000
I mean, there's no more belief than that. He's actually speaking with God.

00:26:43.000 --> 00:26:45.000
It was just in the course of conversation that he did that.

00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:55.000
A man: (unintelligible) Dr. Khalifa: Exactly. Exactly. Yeah.

00:26:57.000 --> 00:26:59.000
Dr. Khalifa: Please stay where you are. I'll be back in one minute.

00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:16.000
[57:19] Those who believed in GOD and His messengers are the saints and martyrs. ...

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:18.000
A woman: Did you just say 504? 504?

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:20.000
Dr. Khalifa: Wow. 540.

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:21.000
A woman: Ok.

00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: The page number is 540.

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:26.000
A woman: Wow. (unintelligible)

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:32.000
Parivash: 57:19 A woman: Yeah.

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:27:35.000 --> 00:27:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is quite a statement. A woman: How?

00:27:37.000 --> 00:27:38.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:40.000
This is quite a statement here. It says,

00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:43.000
[57:19] Those who believed in GOD and His messengers are the saints and martyrs. ...

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:49.000
And all of a sudden it fits to the new information that we got.

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:52.000
That the righteous go straight to Heaven. They do not die.

00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:57.000
Remember the verse that says "do not say about the martyrs that they are dead."

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:04.000
So, martyrs are not only the people who die in battle, fighting.

00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:10.000
People who die believing in God and His messengers are the saints and the martyrs.

00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:20.000
[57:19] ... Reserved for them at their Lord are their rewards and their light. As for those who disbelieved and rejected our revelations, they have incurred Hell.

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:24.000
Preoccupation With This Life Condemned

00:28:25.000 --> 00:28:54.000
[57:20] Know that this worldly life is no more than play and games, and boasting among you, and hoarding of money and children. It is like abundant rain that produces plants and pleases the disbelievers. But then the plants turn into useless hay, and are blown away by the wind. In the Hereafter there is either severe retribution, or forgiveness from GOD and approval. This worldly life is no more than a temporary illusion.

00:28:56.000 --> 00:28:58.000
The Intelligent Alternative

00:28:58.000 --> 00:29:10.000
[57:21] Therefore, you shall race towards forgiveness from your Lord, and a Paradise whose width encompasses the heaven and the earth. It awaits those who believed in GOD and His messengers. ...

00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:13.000
See, this fits with the first line that we read.

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:23.000
The same Paradise where Adam and Eve lived. It awaits each, every righteous person when he or she departs from this world.

00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:28.000
To me, this is very exciting news and we were very excited when that happened.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:36.000
I was so excited that in the same day, I printed that page that you got in the mail and I mailed it.

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:37.000
You get two of them?

00:29:39.000 --> 00:29:41.000
I sent one to your house and one to Batool.

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:44.000
You're the only one I sent two copies to.

00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:51.000
I figured that if you get the two of them you can always pass it on to somebody else.

00:29:54.000 --> 00:30:00.000
But I immediately typed this and sent it and of course that was crucial because

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:04.000
I don't know if Amir Ali knows this or not, but my mother passed away 10 days after that.

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:07.000
Right after that. It was fantastic news.

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:11.000
It's like God is telling us, assuring us because I knew all along that she was a believer.

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:18.000
So, when she passed away and they were dreading telling me on the other end of the line,

00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:20.000
I said "Wow. Alhamdu Lillah. Mã Shã Allãh"

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:23.000
"What's wrong with him?"

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:30.000
Feroz: (unintelligible) They may die but they are in a better place. Dr. Khalifa: Yes. Very. Exactly.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's like she went to a wonderful vacation in Hawaii or something and she's waiting for us until we get there.

00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:45.000
So, but, these, these, and these verses came immediately after that to confirm.

00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:52.000
And I'm telling you it's wonderful because I experienced it.

00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:54.000
I know exactly how it feels.

00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:58.000
Because obviously this is where I went when I met all the Prophets.

00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:00.000
This is where I went.

00:31:10.000 --> 00:31:17.000
I just called the Parivash in my office to listen to some Quran by Sheikh Al-Banna, of my favorite reciter.

00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:18.000
And of course she cried.

00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:24.000
Because it was beautiful mainly. Not just because she's a good believer.

00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:29.000
But this is what I was doing when I experienced that.

00:31:31.000 --> 00:31:34.000
Let me call it righteous death which is not death.

00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:36.000
I was listening to Sheikh Al-Banna. I was listening to it.

00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:41.000
Now, what condition were you in when you were listening to Al-Banna, when you were listening to Al-Banna now?

00:31:43.000 --> 00:31:47.000
Dr. Khalifa: What condition were you in when you were listening to Sheikh Al-Banna in the Parivash: Now?

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:49.000
Dr. Khalifa: when I called you in to listen to the Quran?

00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:52.000
Dr. Khalifa: What condition were you in?

00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:54.000
A woman (Speaking Farsi): How was your mood? Dr. Khalifa: How did you feel?

00:31:54.000 --> 00:31:55.000
Parivash: Well, great.

00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:56.000
Dr. Khalifa: Right.

00:31:57.000 --> 00:31:58.000
Parivash: More than good.

00:31:58.000 --> 00:32:00.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's a state of ecstasy. You know what I mean?

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:04.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is how I felt when all of a sudden I was up there.

00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:08.000
That is exactly equivalent to the death of the righteous.

00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:09.000
Yeah.

00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:10.000
A woman: You were not asleep?

00:32:10.000 --> 00:32:14.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, no. I was not asleep. I will not sleep when Sheikh Al-Banna is reciting.

00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:22.000
God taught me a few things through that experience.

00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:27.000
First of all, I'm a person who does not know what I ate yesterday or even what day was it yesterday.

00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:30.000
Dr. Khalifa: What day is it today? A man: Tuesday.

00:32:31.000 --> 00:32:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: See, would you (unintelligible). Tuesday.

00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:39.000
It's very difficult for me to remember what I did last Thursday, what date it was, things like that.

00:32:40.000 --> 00:32:41.000
I'm very bad with remembering dates.

00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:47.000
But God did it in such a way that I know the day, the date, the time.

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: And that I was awake. A man: What you were listening.

00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because I will never sleep when Sheikh Al-Banna is reciting. He reads only for half hour, 6 o'clock in the morning every Tuesday.

00:32:57.000 --> 00:33:00.000
All his life, this is what he did.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:05.000
All the other reciters in Egypt, the time slot changed, but not Sheikh Al-Banna.

00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:10.000
He only read 6 o'clock in the morning every Tuesday from Cairo Radio.

00:33:10.000 --> 00:33:14.000
A woman: So, it was on the radio? A woman: You were listening to the radio? Dr. Khalifa: Yes. Yes. Yes.

00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:15.000
Dr. Khalifa: I was... A woman: I thought you were reciting the Quran.

00:33:16.000 --> 00:33:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, no, I was listening. So, I, after we Prayed Fajr in the Ka‘bah, then I, we came with my parents.

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:25.000
And then, I tuned into Cairo.

00:33:26.000 --> 00:33:28.000
So, I know the time. It was 6 o'clock in the morning.

00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:30.000
For Sheikh Al-Banna, so, I never go to sleep.

00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: And he was reading Sura Al-Rahmaan.

00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:35.000
A man: Yes.

00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, I was in a state of ecstasy.

00:33:39.000 --> 00:33:44.000
And my brother was recording it. At that very moment, my brother Atif was recording it in Egypt.

00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:47.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, I have a record of it.

00:33:47.000 --> 00:33:48.000
A woman: How long have you been...?

00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:49.000
Dr. Khalifa: I didn't miss it.

00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:55.000
Because when I came back, I knew that Atif recorded it.

00:33:55.000 --> 00:33:57.000
A man: You know date and the year.

00:33:57.000 --> 00:33:59.000
Dr. Khalifa: I know the date, the day was Tuesday.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:04.000
Dr. Khalifa: I know the date, it was December 21st, because my parents and myself spent only one Tuesday in Mecca.

00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:07.000
And it was December 21st.

00:34:07.000 --> 00:34:09.000
Cause I know it was Zul-Hijja 3.

00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:13.000
So, I mean, I know the lunar date, the solar date, the time.

00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:14.000
A woman: It was 1971?

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:17.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, December 21, 1971.

00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:25.000
A woman: I thought we were there in 71, but we were. in Ramadan. And I thought it was November, but I don't think it could be November.

00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, November was Zul-Qaʿdah

00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:31.000
Dr. Khalifa: Zul-Hijja was in December. A woman: (unintelligible) relatives in Medina.

00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:33.000
A woman: We were there for Ramadan.

00:34:34.000 --> 00:34:37.000
A woman: But it should be (unintelligible)

00:34:38.000 --> 00:34:44.000
Dr. Khalifa: If it's Ramadan, then it was October, yes.

00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:48.000
A man: (Unintelligible) December. Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:34:48.000 --> 00:34:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: Of course, December 21 was Zul-Hijja 3.

00:34:54.000 --> 00:34:58.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, it could have been the beginning of November. Yes. A woman: November.

00:34:58.000 --> 00:35:00.000
Feroz: How many Earth minutes went by...?

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.000
Dr. Khalifa: Because it was the end of December, but the beginning of Zul-Hijja.

00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:04.000
Dr. Khalifa: Pardon?

00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:08.000
Feroz: How many, like, how much time went by on Earth, when you, like, came back? Dr. Khalifa: Like one hour.

00:35:08.000 --> 00:35:10.000
Feroz: About one hour. Dr. Khalifa: Yeah.

00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:14.000
Feroz: But did you feel you were there for quite a while?

00:35:15.000 --> 00:35:17.000
Feroz: Did you feel you were there for quite a while?

00:35:18.000 --> 00:35:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, it was quite an elaborate introduction.

00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:26.000
It was quite a procession of people, going this way.

00:35:26.000 --> 00:35:29.000
Feroz: And they were all prophets? Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:31.000
Feroz: (unintelligible)

00:35:34.000 --> 00:35:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: I didn't count. I didn't...

00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:38.000
A woman: Do you remember every detail of it or was it...?

00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: It was very sharp.

00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: The consciousness was very sharp.

00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:43.000
A woman: Like they...

00:35:43.000 --> 00:35:45.000
Dr. Khalifa: Sharper than what we're doing now.

00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:48.000
A woman: So, you saw everything in detail?

00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: I saw the persons. I didn't see surroundings.

00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:55.000
And God showed them to me in their worldly looks.

00:35:55.000 --> 00:35:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: What they're dressed like here in this world.

00:35:57.000 --> 00:35:59.000
Feroz: Do all look different in their faces?

00:35:59.000 --> 00:36:00.000
Dr. Khalifa: Oh yeah, they all looked different.

00:36:01.000 --> 00:36:04.000
I was taken aback by Abraham's resemblance to my family.

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:07.000
"Wow, who's this guy who looks like us?"

00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:10.000
It was all in my mind, and the answer came in my mind also.

00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:11.000
"This is Abraham."

00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:13.000
